// timeseries/ — classical statistical time-series models.
//
// The recurrences themselves need only core: given y and p coefficients, the
// next value is a dot product. Estimating the coefficients needs more, and
// that is where analysis/ comes in -- Yule-Walker solves for AR coefficients
// via the autocovariance function, so ts_pacf, ts_diff_n, ts_cumsum and
// ts_mean are part of the fitting path rather than an optional extra. None of
// it touches a tensor, a parameter block or an optimiser.
//
// arima.mbt is the one with substance -- Yule-Walker closed-form coefficients,
// differencing, ACF/PACF estimation -- and the other three exist to be
// building blocks for it: AR(p) is ARMA(p, 0), MA(q) is ARMA(0, q). They stay
// as separate files because they are separately useful, not because they are
// separately large.
//
// ar_debug.mbt holds the diagnostic printouts, arima_demo.mbt the end-to-end
// fit-and-forecast pipeline. Both are development aids rather than API, and
// both stay here rather than in examples/ because time_series_ensemble.mbt
// drives arima_demo directly.
//
// `time_series_ensemble.mbt` does not move in: it combines forecasts from
// several of these models, so it consumes this package rather than belonging
// to it.
import {
  "riantr/snn_mbt/core",
  "riantr/snn_mbt/analysis",
}
